# Hostile audit — defect-charged train freedom and rank barrier

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Status:** audited-working proof-only material; theorem state unchanged  
**Audited source:** [defect-charged train freedom and exact locking-rank barrier](target_c_defect_charged_train_flex_and_rank_barrier.md)

## Verdict

The physical-boundary identities, injective hole charge, train-angle flex lower bound,
outer-to-outer shear count, and Maxwell row-count identity are valid on the
nonisolated positive-contact core under the stated stopped-train hypotheses. The final
row-count comparison is intentionally a no-go result: it proves that nominal external
row count alone cannot contradict mixed rigidity. It does not close C-II.

## Checks

1. Face incidence gives 4R=2(E_R-P_R)+P_R, hence E_R=2R+T, and Euler on the
   finite rhombus cell complex gives V_R=R+T+c_R-g_R. These formulas use edge
   occurrences and remain valid with bridges, holes, and vertex-touching components.

2. A physical boundary occurrence on a bounded hole has a bounded contact face on its
   other side. It cannot be another strict rhombus, or it would belong to the same
   rhombus union. Since all bounded quadrilateral contact faces are strict rhombi, the
   opposite face is nonquadrilateral. The map from hole occurrences to nonquadrilateral
   face-edge incidences is injective, giving P_hole<=4f+Q.

3. A hole of length one or two is impossible in a simple straight-line contact graph.
   A four-edge hole is an equilateral quadrilateral, hence a unit rhombus; the standard
   triangle-free rhombus coverage lemma then makes it an actual quadrilateral contact
   face, not a complementary hole. Therefore each hole has at least five boundary
   occurrences and 5g_R<=4f+Q.

4. For each edge-connected rhombus component, train angular rates have at most two
   vector period constraints per hole. The kernel dimension is at least T_C-2g_C.
   Summing gives dim F_train>=T-2g_R, and the hole bound yields the printed
   T-(2/5)(4f+Q) estimate.

5. A train with no hole endpoint is outer-to-outer. Hence the count of such trains is
   at least T-P_hole, and therefore at least T-(4f+Q). Rotating only that train
   vector closes every rhombus and leaves all hole periods zero; the statement is
   limited to the rhombus subframework and does not assert preservation of external
   bars.

6. The Maxwell floor dim ker R_R>=2V_R-E_R=T+2c_R-2g_R follows directly from
   rank at most the number of rhombus bars. With x=m-V_R, the mixed row count
   gives the exact difference
   N_ext-[(2V_R-E_R)-r_x]=2x-2+s_Z+r_x; substituting the three values of r_x
   yields at least 1+s_Z in every case.

## Limits

- The hole-length-four step depends on the canonical empty-strict-rhombus coverage
  lemma; it is not a generic statement about arbitrary four-point polygons.
- The train-angle count is first-order, and finite one-train shears are asserted only
  for outer-to-outer trains in the rhombus subframework.
- The external-row difference is an exact nominal count. It does not bound the rank of
  external rows restricted to train shears, nor does it give a small-singular-value
  estimate.
- Contact-isolated source points remain outside the core matrices.
- No Type-I augmentation, global minimum-diameter implication, or Level-I result is
  claimed.

**Claim classification:** audited-working exact structural/no-go theorem; proof-only
research candidate; C-II remains open.

